---
description: Rules for Cursor implementation workers in price-memo
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow price-memo/AGENTS.md before non-trivial changes. Stay within
the assigned work order and this repository.

- price-memo is a strict unit-price comparison and shopping memo app.
- Preserve exact weight, quantity, and volume semantics. Never promote guessed
  or approximate values to confirmed data.
- Do not add household expense management or AI expense categorization.
- Shared Supabase migrations are managed only in
  receipt-manager/supabase/migrations/. Never create, retain, or apply
  migrations from price-memo; never run a database push.
- Do not edit receipt-manager or any other repository from a price-memo worker
  task. If work appears to require another repository, schema change, or
  architectural decision, stop and report the reason and evidence to the
  supervisor.
- Do not silently change public API contracts.
- Prefer small, focused changes and avoid unrelated refactors.
- Run `npm run check` after implementation.
- For browser/UI work, use Playwright when it materially verifies the task.

At completion, report:
- root cause / implementation intent
- changed files
- verification results
- remaining risks
- anything requiring supervisor review
